ng the town. Once he was old enough to care for himself he began, after each attack, to set from the village to find and punish those that hurt his home.<br /> <br /> It was on one of these trips that he exalted as a chosen of Luna. Cornered by several scavengers he talked despretaly, hoping to convince them to spare him. As he spoke he found the words coming easier to him, the arguements more persuasive and his efforts more successful. The resulting fight, as some scavengers sought to release him and some sought to kill him, gave Jarsiln the perfect opportunity to sneak away to safety.<br /> <br /> Over the next year Jarsiln tracked, infiltrated and then killed all of the nearby scavenger and bandit groups. He might have stayed in the village, but for the image of the Tyrant Sun standing over a beaten and injured Luna that had burned itself into his memory during his exaltion. Driven by the same desire to punish those that injure others, Jarsiln set out to join the other exalted and punish the Tyrant Sun for his crimes.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <b><u>BP/Starting Exp Spending</u></b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Bonus Points spent: 18<ul><li>First Strength Excellency (5 bp);</li> <li>Relentless Lunar Fury (5 bp);</li> <li>Thrown 3-5 (2bp);</li> <li>Dodge 3-4 (2bp);</li> <li>Stealth 3-4 (2 bp); and</li> <li>Presence 2-3 (2 bp).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> Starting Exp spent: 48/50<ul><li>Essence 2-3 (18 exp);</li> <li>Manipulation 3-4 (9 exp);</li> <li>Mirror Sight Dismay (10 exp); and</li> <li>Falling Leaf Distraction (10 exp).</li> </ul><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","user":"kelsyk","date":". 06-12-2014, 01:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T16:49:24-07:00","id":143942,"title":"","content":"Looks good, Kelsyk. What arm of the Gunstar Military will he be part of?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T16:54:06-07:00","id":143944,"title":"","content":"Nice character Kelsyk looking forward to seeing him in action as for your intimacies Zekka would be a good intimacy as he is a person as well as the ship and for your background point well there is the Solar bond that is a useful thing but that would mean to bond with either Amelia or Pellias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T08:47:49-07:00","id":145688,"title":"","content":"Alright, Kelsyk, Jariln has been introduced. You're free to act now.<br /> <br /> (If you can't think of intimacies, It's fine. You can fill them in later. I won't hold it against you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T09:53:06-07:00","id":145774,"title":"","content":"Jarsiln is a member of the Void Hunt, I don't know which, if any, part of the Solar Deliberative military that is part of. Within that group he focuses mainly on hunting down and destroying scavenger and bandit groups, especially those that support the Apostates. Jarsiln sees those groups and their actions as continuations of the Tyrant Sun's crimes.<br /> <br /> How did my character join the adventure? Was he recently transfered from the Gunstar or was he operating seperately from the other characters and only now started interacting with them?<br /> <br /> I'll try and catch up on the current situation as fast as possible and post. Before that, does my character know anything about the situation that the others do not at the current time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T10:21:01-07:00","id":145795,"title":"","content":"What I assumed (And thought was a neat idea) was that Jarsiln was in deep cover as part of a scout operation into the Spiral parallel to the operation the other members of the Circle are in. This goes well with him being and infiltrator, and allows you to get into the thick of things ASAP. If he's part of the Void Hunt, he'd be assuredly a section of the Gunstar Military's Intelligence/Political Officer Corps, so he'd probably be familiar, or at least know OF Jin (Noodle's Character) and Wren (Palemask's character).<br /> <br /> (Spoiler'd so other people aren't immediately wise to OoC info they're not privy to yet)<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> He'd also be aware of the existence, at this point, of the true purpose of the complex. He's been here a few days longer than the Circle, I'm thinking, and has seen more than one Gauntlet go on. Sable Thesis Dream has built this complex, not only as a temple to Metagaos, the Ever-Hunger Blossom, but also built it as a means of studying, and potentially mass-producing circumstances to Exalt mortals. That she's only succeeded once suggests that she's still in the preliminary phases of her experiment. </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T10:31:04-07:00","id":145800,"title":"","content":"OKay, I will try to be caught up and post later today (I am at GMT -5).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T23:29:14-07:00","id":146451,"title":"","content":"Sorry that took me so long-I got really sick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T07:33:25-07:00","id":146719,"title":"","content":"It's all good, Palemask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T19:11:34-07:00","id":147436,"title":"","content":"Hey Kelsyk, welcome aboard! Just wanted to clarify about the Solar Mate thing as I think it deserves a bit more attention than a throwaway point. I'm open to the idea of being a Solar Mate, but I'd prefer it to be a bit more detailed in our respective backgrounds, more especially if you were on infiltration assignment and have been gone for so long. Take a read of my fiction sample on my sheet: does the hunt scenario resonate with what you were thinking at all?<br /> <br /> As for the core, it's an adapted Panopticon Stone from the Ink Monkeys (Infernal Hearthstone). The Infernal Version lets one make Eyes of Orabilis (floating eye scanners that feed right back to the owner); I figured that the Autochthonian version would make more robotic or probe-like eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T22:07:04-07:00","id":147582,"title":"","content":"That's probably a good idea. Do either of your characters share a common history, or is this the first time you've met?<br /> <br /> Also, this is one of the things I've realized about Gunstar; that many details I take for granted in Vanilla Exalted that aren't true here, like Vitriol not being Vitriol. Yet. Still being Thien-To, it is a powerful transmutive acid, with dangerous, destructive potential, but also powerful potential to refine and perfect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T10:54:58-07:00","id":147970,"title":"","content":"The way I see my character this is likely the first time they have met. Jarsiln prefers operating alone amoung the populations of the reaches. Mainly this is because Jarsiln enjoys the feeling of power he gets from using his abilities and charms on people. However he would feel guilty about using those abilities on loyal citizens of the realm, which is why he prefers not to operate in the realm.<br /> <br /> The hunt scenario described doesn't really fit with how I see the character. His focus on social charms and stealth would be more benefit dealing with apostates and disgruntled citizens then hunting monsters on some planet. He volunteered for the infiltration assignment more ebcause of the opportunity to get close to the Tyrant Sun than because he though his skills would be particularily well suited.<br /> <br /> I imagened that Jarsiln would have been inserted into creation atleast several weeks, probably months before the main mission began. This was to allow time to gather intelligence and so that if the scouts were detected they were less likely to compromise the main missions entrance.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I missed something but don't hearthsontes require a Manse, and the section describing backgrounds in Gunstar says that Manse cannot be created in Autochtonia. So how does you character have a hearthstone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T14:14:42-07:00","id":148113,"title":"","content":"Damn, that was lucky but <i>ouch</i>, that roll. The effects? Totally worth it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T15:40:58-07:00","id":148198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kelsyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=147970#post147970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I missed something but don't hearthsontes require a Manse, and the section describing backgrounds in Gunstar says that Manse cannot be created in Autochtonia. So how does you character have a hearthstone?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's not a hearthstone, it's an elemental core that has the same mechanical effect as a published Hearthstone. My character has several like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T22:35:49-07:00","id":148398,"title":"","content":"I can jive with the social/intelligence aspect of your character; I will try to come up with something creative when the weekend is past me a bit. I will raise, however, that Autocthonian Realm Exalted culture seems a bit tight, so much so that I'd put forward that it's unlikely that something as important as meeting your Solar-Lunar mate would be something done by chance outside of Autocthon. I mean, hell... I figure someone would at least suggest we meet for a coffee/beer <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T07:04:30-07:00","id":148674,"title":"","content":"I don't think it that strange given our characters backgrounds. Your character seems to prefers operating as part of the scouting expeditions outside Autochthon, my character prefers to operate alone in the reaches within Autochthon. Combined with both our characters youth it is not inconceivable that they would not have run into each other. Unless each exalted is taken around and introduced to all the other exalted, or the Sidereal regularily use astrology to determine the Solar-Lunar bond and arrange for their meeting. I don't mind coming up with something about a previous meeting, but I don't see it as neccesary and it could be interesting to play through the story as our character get to know each other and figure out the dynamics of their bond.<br /> <br /> Other than Astrology (I assume that would work) and meeting through random chance, is there any other way to determine who the Solar or Lunar are bonded to?<br /> <br /> Thanks for clearing up the elemental cores, I must have missed that section when I read the Alchemical book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T13:47:31-07:00","id":148918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Palemask</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=148113#post148113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Damn, that was lucky but <i>ouch</i>, that roll. The effects? Totally worth it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I had an evil, EVIL grin on with that roll, ready to grant some terrible agonizing, acid-poison-y doom. However, I then remembered about the whole Thien-To&gt; Vitirol deal, and how Thien-To is a passive, transmuting acid, as opposed to liquid hate. Hence, what happened. Also, if you want to KEEP that internal bonus, you're going to need to keep applying it. Or find some way of internalizing Thien-To's inherent transmutation into your body.<br /> <br /> As for your question, Kelsyk, there's Astrology, Lytek, Readings of Samsara, Beseeching Ess'Tee, the Dark Constellation, for information, and of course, asking Luna or Sol about it. Some of those are more possible than others, but I imagine it could be done easily enough if the Exalt put their mind to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 05-25-2014, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T14:42:27-07:00","id":148943,"title":"","content":"I'm surprise he's still alive those were good hits but I think Wren's is in big trouble though, I should thank you Dietaku you are giving me everything I wanted in a gunstar exalted game so thanks a lot. Fighting against that hellstrider makes me think of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f3bHENs9-2A\" target=\"_blank\">that </a>if you've played the game and liked it you know what I'm talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T15:01:28-07:00","id":148970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=148943#post148943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprise he's still alive those were good hits but I think Wren's is in big trouble though, I should thank you Dietaku you are giving me everything I wanted in a gunstar exalted game so thanks a lot. Fighting against that hellstrider makes me think of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=f3bHENs9-2A\" target=\"_blank\">that </a>if you've played the game and liked it you know what I'm talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like it, and Gunstar offers a lot more chances to use some of the crazier things that Exalted offers. Warstriders are one of those, as even common warstriders are terrifying, dangerous machines that can tip a entire conflict towards their favor. However, in Gunstar, they're one of a myriad of tools.<br /> <br /> (Also, I haven't played Revengence. I've heard a lot about it, and it looks fun. However, (And this is going into headcanon time here) the hell/warstriders that I've employed are all about <i> Overman King Gainer</i>-style in appearance. Odd, more organic than robot-y, and not nearly as gigantic as Gundam would make you think of giant robots. The Archemizer is a loving tribute to this series, being a take on the Dominator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T15:45:00-07:00","id":148979,"title":"","content":"Doesn't ring a bell but I'll check it out haven't watch anime in years, also you told us that Zekka was outfitted with two factory cathedral does that means we could request for artifacts to be built for us and if we can how would it be handled in you game term do we pay XP for them or ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T11:02:37-07:00","id":149554,"title":"","content":"Man, Wren is just not doing well in this fight. /laughs and cries at Wren<br /> <br /> Still, I find it somewhat hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T16:30:22-07:00","id":149793,"title":"","content":"Yes, you can commission artifacts, Magnusar (Hell, that's one of the Commissariat Division's given functions), but you'll need to acquire the materials to build them. I don't usually require Exp to get backgrounds, as often-times, my players role-play out getting such assets.<br /> <br /> Actually, I think that Wren has performed admirably considering how far out of his specialty he is right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T17:05:57-07:00","id":149827,"title":"","content":"I think so too Wren is not a fighter after all. It's good to know that we can get new stuff though how do we know what to get the division gives you a shopping list or something.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T08:07:46-07:00","id":150354,"title":"","content":"Question about the artifact background in gunstar: Is each artifact bought seperately (and excess points lost such as buying a 2 point artifact) or does purchasing the artifact background provide a pool or points for aquiring artifacts (in which case I did my character wrong and have an extra background point or 3 artifact points left)?<br /> <br /> Question about magical materials and artifacts: do all artifact weapons and armour automatically have one of the magical materials or are they purchased seperately for additional cost? If the magical material is included, does that also apply to specific artifacts (such as the Everyman Armour)? When using a thrown weapon in melee combat does it continue to use the benefits listed on p.389 for Ranged use of the Five Magical Materials, or does it gain the benefits on p.387 for Melee with the Five Magical Materials?<br /> <br /> Questions about Lunar shape shifting: the section about the war form specifically mentions that moonsilver armour will shift to accomodate the new shape, but the section on the spirit form does not mention it either way; will moonsilver armour shift to fit the spirit form of a Lunar? Would a smaller form (such as Jarsiln's bobcat or mouse form) provide bonuses to dodge due to size?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","user":"kelsyk","date":". 05-27-2014, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:07:37-07:00","id":150418,"title":"","content":"Answer to Question 1: Here we have Janus Q. Solar. Janus is a Gunstar character, and an affable enough chap. Let's say he's a Zenith Caste General. Janus wants a distinctive weapon, and one that also could assist in his generalship. He settles on the Third Arm Glaive (From Storyteller's Companion), a potent artifact spear which doubles as a banner for mass combat. However, the Glaive is a five dot artifact; that's pretty hefty, even for the Glaive's impressive benefits. HOWEVER! Because of Janus' Artifact 5 rating, he gets an effective 15(!) points in artifacts he can buy, so he could easily buy a set of power armor or another weapon, or possibly even a warstrider, even WITH his Third Arm Glaive. Y'see, Artifact in Gunstar works as it does for Alchemicals, which get an effective three for one rate of purchasing artifacts for background dots.If you didn't take this into account, it's cool.Just add whatever you want and have points for to your sheet, and everything will be even.<br /> <br /> Answer to Question 2: They often do, but sometimes they don't. The outliers are usually powerful or strange items from the Wyld or are Helltech from Malfeas. Such things are made out of Gossamer (The stuff of Dreams made into a tangible form) or demon flesh and Vitriol (Malfeas' one element, a form of passive consumptive acid which due to Malfeas' mutilation, became liquid hate and anger. Here in Gunstar, however, it is a powerful alchemical reagent, known as Thien-To.)<br /> <br /> It doesn't cost any more to purchase items made out of the Magical Materials at Chargen; after all, that's partly what makes them artifacts in the first place, and so you can just say ,&quot; Oh, yeah, my Daiklaive is made out of Orichalcum. No biggie&quot; and most, if not all STs will go, &quot;Okay, yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, MAKING artifacts in-character, on the other hand, is a different matter. To do so, you need to have magical materials, or exotic materials, on hand, and to make the alloys necessary for the magical materials is a long, expensive process in and of itself. Oadnael's Codex goes over it far better than I could.<br /> <br /> As per your last question, let's go back to Janus Q. Solar again. Janus has an artifact Francisa, an axe made for both throwing and for use as a melee weapon, constructed out of Orichalcum, made by hist bestest buddy Golden T. Alchemicalbot. Should Janus decide to toss that sumbitch at a demon, it'd have the Orichalcum bonus for thrown weapons. Should he decide to bury it in the demon's face with a strike, it'd have the melee bonus. Does that mean it has BOTH bonuses? Well, yes, and no. You only get one benefit at a time depending on what you're using it for, and weapons which allow such options are rare (The Vajra spear in Scroll of the Monk comes to mind.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully, that answers all your questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T15:56:40-07:00","id":150864,"title":"","content":"This is not going to end well I think but then again nothing ends well with us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like Zephyr as an enemy even if I do not really understand what is her purpose. Murder to liberate the unthinking masses ? All I understood is that she's like the inquisition hunting the heretics or something like that. Could you explain a bit Dietaku or would that be too much spoilers ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T17:09:37-07:00","id":150896,"title":"","content":"Shenanigans done. c:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T18:58:20-07:00","id":150946,"title":"","content":"Not sure what you did there but whatever that was I hope it works ( I haven't read the book on sids yet)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:44:49-07:00","id":151288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=150864#post150864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is not going to end well I think but then again nothing ends well with us <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I like Zephyr as an enemy even if I do not really understand what is her purpose. Murder to liberate the unthinking masses ? All I understood is that she's like the inquisition hunting the heretics or something like that. Could you explain a bit Dietaku or would that be too much spoilers ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hahahaha, Using Chains of Adorjan on Zephyr, and expecting her to die? Tell the audience, Noodle, how did that work out last time?<br /> <br /> Sarcasm aside, Zephyr is a interesting and complex person to be sure. She's actually an NPC from another game, whereby she was the muscle of a trio of GSPs (Sable Thesis Dream, Flawless Acacia, and herself). There was a zealot Zenith caste then that hated her to no end, and because of this, she took his advances as feelings of true love. Things progressed...Well, I'll let Noodle say that.<br /> <br /> As for her motivations, one has to realize that she's pretty insane, even disregarding her Adorjani charms which alter human perceptions (Murder is Meat, Tragic Love Amusement, etc.) and her sense of logic and thought isn't entirely natural nor normal. Her self-proscribed &quot;mission&quot; is to slay those who do not understand the Truth; that all life is painful, and that in order to prevent this, one must remove all earthly attachments, and train a sense of proper spiritual understanding. Being not entirely rational, and possessing a unique holy air ever since she was small, she's actually quite easy to manipulate, and rationalizes much of what is told to her through the lens of ,&quot;Well, I'm helping them get closer to the truth, even if I'm killing them now,&quot; hence your understanding of her as this inquisitor-type. She's not really an inquisitor at heart, but rather, she's used to that end by her colleagues.<br /> <br /> I hope that answers your question, Magnusar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T07:58:02-07:00","id":151303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=151288#post151288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hahahaha, Using Chains of Adorjan on Zephyr, and expecting her to die? Tell the audience, Noodle, how did that work out last time?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Dietaku, that's a hard one. <br /> <br /> She survived, started hitting on the Circle's Zenith, and dashed of into the Sunset. She then reappeared when we went to Autochthonia, having dyed her hair blue, and changed her name to &quot;Cerulean Cloud&quot;. She was missing her voice and one of her arms, the former of which she had traded to a Fae to turn the blood she had from the Zenith into a pound of flesh. The later was a payment to demon flesh-smiths to forge aforesaid pound of flesh and a pound of her own flesh into a behemoth/half-caste/demon-blood kid. <br /> <br /> Shit was wack.<br /> <br /> Anyways, if future events follow past performance, Wren has just doomed Amelia to eternity as the focus of this particular Scourge's affections. <br /> <br /> Fun times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T12:16:26-07:00","id":151577,"title":"","content":"Oh, boy. Wren is just glad to be alive for the moment! If exhausted. COA took all his endurance, so he'd be at -1 Endurance. He's going to be useless or fainted for the rest of that scene but still-for a non-fighter Sidereal, that was a badass way to end a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T14:01:48-07:00","id":151662,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Palemask</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=150896#post150896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shenanigans done. c:</div> </div> </div> </div>That was one hell of a shenanigan O.O !!! And don't worry Palemask Amelia will take very good care of Wren while he is unconscious or will she <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-28-2014, 05:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T21:43:54-07:00","id":152100,"title":"","content":"Question regarding Jin/the DaevaMechs: how long are you ruling it would take to attune? If Jin is hopping inside, is there simply a quick attunement surge and then he's off to the races, or is this something that would likely take a few minutes (and need a bit of time without distraction from the DENNISes)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T07:16:04-07:00","id":152479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jotun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=152100#post152100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question regarding Jin/the DaevaMechs: how long are you ruling it would take to attune? If Jin is hopping inside, is there simply a quick attunement surge and then he's off to the races, or is this something that would likely take a few minutes (and need a bit of time without distraction from the DENNISes)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that these weapons are objects of boredom, and not meant to be personalized items for any one Exalt, there will be a mechanism in the cockpit to allow for quick attunement and deployment. That being said, the cockpits themselves aren't uniform, and may take some getting used to. Depending on your (Wits+Ride/Sail) roll, you could either be off, or stumble around, earning a penalty for a few rounds as you over/undercompensate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T11:35:00-07:00","id":152735,"title":"","content":"Okay okay, fellow infiltration team members- <br /> <br /> My plan is for Jin to take one of the Warstriders, then you guys can break off to get the others while Jin covers you. <br /> <br /> Knowing that our ST is a major mecha fanboy, my educated guess is that Pellias should take the black-and-gold robot, while Jariln takes the red-jade one. Just my thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T13:06:41-07:00","id":152878,"title":"","content":"I do not dispute the claim of my being a &quot;Mecha fanboy,&quot; just that isn't everyone a little? Giant robots are awesome!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:01:40-07:00","id":152948,"title":"","content":"How many motes do I have to commit to attune to the Turnx?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:04:39-07:00","id":152952,"title":"","content":"It costs 12 motes to attune to the Tannicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:05:25-07:00","id":152954,"title":"","content":"Okay. Good to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:28:24-07:00","id":152975,"title":"","content":"Now I'm kinda jealous Noodle you got the cool toys lol. Dietaku what just happened Airi just exploded for no reason ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-29-2014, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:42:45-07:00","id":153018,"title":"","content":"Well, you know how Flawless Acacia had all those arrows which disappeared?<br /> <br /> NONE OF THOSE MISSED. Just thought you'd want to know that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T14:58:25-07:00","id":153088,"title":"","content":"Okay... well now that he's missing arm it will be a bit difficult to fire arrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:19:44-07:00","id":153288,"title":"","content":"I'm actually going to go sideways on this and -not- jump in a mech, unless, Dietaku, this causes you to groan and mutter <i>stop making this difficult and just take the damn robot... </i>Would be sabotaging the bloody things if Pellias had the skill to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T17:22:33-07:00","id":153291,"title":"","content":"NOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! lol Actually this is a rare opportunity for study and getting our hands on powerful equipment but then again Amelia is not there so it's your call Jotun","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 05-29-2014, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:11:28-07:00","id":153342,"title":"","content":"Put it this way: Pellias isn't great at being up front for too long and self-sufficiency is a minor theme of his. Add this to questionable technology that keeps attacking him (see ye DENNIS and ye <i>Zekka</i>) and he's more likely to really raise an eyebrow at hooking up in a suit he's not certain he can control or get out of. Better to burn than to learn when pressed for time.<br /> <br /> That being said, I'm all for the fact that this is a storytelling exercise and that sometimes the ST throws a plot-line bone at you that ceases to be fun if the paranoia of the PC (and the player) makes it into something it isn't (ex: <i>&quot;You see a door&quot; &quot;I check for traps&quot; &quot;no traps&quot; &quot;I check for magic traps&quot; &quot;no magic traps&quot; &quot;I listen for dangerous sounds&quot;.....*</i>many minutes later* .... <i>&quot;JUST OPEN THE DAMN DOOR!&quot;</i>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:17:27-07:00","id":153349,"title":"","content":"That I do understand well considering Pellias job it is normal that he would look for ways to cripple the things there is also the fact that we are far behind enemy lines so it's not too much of a stretch that he would use it we are against overwhelming odds after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T07:59:58-07:00","id":153839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jotun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=153288#post153288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm actually going to go sideways on this and -not- jump in a mech, unless, Dietaku, this causes you to groan and mutter <i>stop making this difficult and just take the damn robot... </i>Would be sabotaging the bloody things if Pellias had the skill to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I'm fine with it. The conversation which prompted their inclusion went a little something like this<br /> <br /> Me: (Thinking) I need something to connect the two parties. I know! I'll have Zephyr zoom by, singing some mecha theme song! Hmm. That means that the corridor is large enough to accommodate her hellstrider, and I'll probably have a shutter on one end. Yeah.<br /> Noodle: So, if this is the lowest level, and there's a large corridor to allow passage of hellstriders, the hangar must be nearby!<br /> Me: ...Yes.<br /> Noodle: So, is Graubarg the Great there, then?<br /> Me: Um. I guess?<br /> Noodle: Great! I'mma--<br /> Me: HIJACK IT AND DIE!<br /> Noodle: Fine. I won't take it, then.<br /> Me: Good.<br /> Noodle: I'll make Pellias do it!<br /> Me: ...Fine.<br /> <br /> (For reference, Graubarg the Great is Sable Thesis Dream's personal Hellstrider she used in her prior appearances)<br /> <br /> In short, I needed to have variety to prevent Noodle from hijacking Graubarg, and I also couldn't pass up a chance to put in a nod to my favorite <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1pYduET6PwI\" target=\"_blank\">mecha series</a>. So, I'm fine with you not taking one, and respect your decision to do so based off Pellias' personality. As for grumbling about ,&quot;Not getting it,&quot; I try to not force players into those situations, and am amused/ intrigued oftentiems by unusual or unconventional solutions, and do my best to accommodate them. This is supposed to be fun for everyone, after all, not just me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T11:41:08-07:00","id":154065,"title":"","content":"lol Wren doesn't rest /cries at","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T09:25:01-07:00","id":154897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=150418#post150418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Answer to Question 1: Here we have Janus Q. Solar. Janus is a Gunstar character, and an affable enough chap. Let's say he's a Zenith Caste General. Janus wants a distinctive weapon, and one that also could assist in his generalship. He settles on the Third Arm Glaive (From Storyteller's Companion), a potent artifact spear which doubles as a banner for mass combat. However, the Glaive is a five dot artifact; that's pretty hefty, even for the Glaive's impressive benefits. HOWEVER! Because of Janus' Artifact 5 rating, he gets an effective 15(!) points in artifacts he can buy, so he could easily buy a set of power armor or another weapon, or possibly even a warstrider, even WITH his Third Arm Glaive. Y'see, Artifact in Gunstar works as it does for Alchemicals, which get an effective three for one rate of purchasing artifacts for background dots.If you didn't take this into account, it's cool.Just add whatever you want and have points for to your sheet, and everything will be even.<br /> <br /> Answer to Question 2: They often do, but sometimes they don't. The outliers are usually powerful or strange items from the Wyld or are Helltech from Malfeas. Such things are made out of Gossamer (The stuff of Dreams made into a tangible form) or demon flesh and Vitriol (Malfeas' one element, a form of passive consumptive acid which due to Malfeas' mutilation, became liquid hate and anger. Here in Gunstar, however, it is a powerful alchemical reagent, known as Thien-To.)<br /> <br /> It doesn't cost any more to purchase items made out of the Magical Materials at Chargen; after all, that's partly what makes them artifacts in the first place, and so you can just say ,&quot; Oh, yeah, my Daiklaive is made out of Orichalcum. No biggie&quot; and most, if not all STs will go, &quot;Okay, yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, MAKING artifacts in-character, on the other hand, is a different matter. To do so, you need to have magical materials, or exotic materials, on hand, and to make the alloys necessary for the magical materials is a long, expensive process in and of itself. Oadnael's Codex goes over it far better than I could.<br /> <br /> As per your last question, let's go back to Janus Q. Solar again. Janus has an artifact Francisa, an axe made for both throwing and for use as a melee weapon, constructed out of Orichalcum, made by hist bestest buddy Golden T. Alchemicalbot. Should Janus decide to toss that sumbitch at a demon, it'd have the Orichalcum bonus for thrown weapons. Should he decide to bury it in the demon's face with a strike, it'd have the melee bonus. Does that mean it has BOTH bonuses? Well, yes, and no. You only get one benefit at a time depending on what you're using it for, and weapons which allow such options are rare (The Vajra spear in Scroll of the Monk comes to mind.)<br /> <br /> Hopefully, that answers all your questions.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answers, but you didn't answer my questions about Lunar shapeshifting. Does moonsilver shift to fit any alternate form or just the war form? Do smaller sizes provide bonuses to dodge or stealth?<br /> <br /> I had an idea for an artifact that I want feedback on (I haven't read the section on creating artifacts yet so it probably isn't perfect).<br /> <br /> Weapon Wielding Essence Harness<br /> Cost: 2<br /> Attunement: 1<br /> Effect:<br /> When in an alternate form, a Lunar may wield a weapon for which the form lacks the strength or appendages to properly wield. The weapon must be an artifact for which the exalted is attuned. The weapon is wielded using essence based telekenisis, so permanent essence is used in place of the form's strength. The harness can only wield a single weapon, but may use two handed weapons as easily as single handed weapons.<br /> Notes:<br /> The restrictions are to try and keep the attunement cost as low as possible (since Jarsiln is rapidly running out of spare essence).<br /> If allowed I will purchase it with the extra artifact points Jarsiln currently has and pick it up next time he is on the ship. The reasoning being that he commisioned the artifact before begining the infiltration and had them store it on the ship for when he met up with the rest of the team.<br /> <br /> IC reason for artifact:<br /> Jarsiln will likely spend much of his time in animal forms, so artifacts that can help survive in those forms are very useful.<br /> <br /> OOC reason for artifact:<br /> I find the image of Jarsiln entered battle as a tiny mouse wielding a large metal boomerang hilarious. It also opens up the possibility of my riding one of the other characters into battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3025,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","user":"kelsyk","date":". 05-31-2014, 12:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T22:03:27-07:00","id":155444,"title":"","content":"Ah, sorry, I appreciate you reminding me. I've always been in groups who allowed Moonsilver armor to benefit a Lunar in any form, regardless. That's kinda what it does, being as Protean as the Lunar is. It may not be overtly apparent (Unless you really find the idea of a mouse in silver chain-mail to be appealing, which I kinda do now that I think about it), it does protect its user. As for whether small forms provide stealth benefits or not, it depends on the form. For the bobcat and rat forms you asked about specifically, I'd say that rat provides a +2 dodge bonus due to being so small, and bobcat is +2 to stealth and athletics, being an ambush hunter an all. <br /> <br /> Also, from one Lunar player to another, here are some tips:<br /> <br /> -Gift charms and Deadly Beastman are your friends. Don't let those Terrible Argent folks tell you otherwise.<br /> -Dexterity and Wits are bullshit in how good they are, while Manipulation and Appearance are for Trolls who wish to use Troll-fu.<br /> -Stamina makes you nigh-unkillable, and is always good to dip into.<br /> -Alternate forms are <i>alway</i>s an opportunity for stunting.<br /> <br /> Also, your harness is fine, as it reminded me of Breath of Fire, and that is always a good thing. I hope that answers all your concerns, and if you need anything else, don't hesitate to ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T11:52:05-07:00","id":155792,"title":"","content":"Wait keening as in lamenting for the dead ? This is going to be interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T17:10:04-07:00","id":156092,"title":"","content":"I deliberately didn't choose Deadly Beastman because it didn't realy fit with the character concept I had. I put my Manipulation and Appearance as high as they are under the assumption that there would be plenty of opportunity for social interaction with the natives; gathering intelligence and convincing them to rebel, for example. If there is going to be less socail stuff and more combat then I will have to adjust my plans for how I advance Jarsiln.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3025-kelsyk","name":"kelsyk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-02T08:01:49-07:00","id":156526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kelsyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=156092#post156092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I deliberately didn't choose Deadly Beastman because it didn't realy fit with the character concept I had. I put my Manipulation and Appearance as high as they are under the assumption that there would be plenty of opportunity for social interaction with the natives; gathering intelligence and convincing them to rebel, for example. If there is going to be less socail stuff and more combat then I will have to adjust my plans for how I advance Jarsiln.</div> </div> </div> </div>I should elaborate; I wasn't saying that Manipulation and Appearance are bad, just that playing a Manipulation/Appearance Lunar means you fight through trickery and feints as opposed to raw power like most other Exalts. Thus, instead of Wolverine, you are Spider-Man. Or Joseph Joestar. Or Batman. Whichever.<br /> <br /> In that case, try getting Butterfly Eyes Fist or Hypnotic Cobra Method, Both are great social charms that also serve one well in combat as well. Sad to say it, but this game is gonna have a lot of combat. Not that It would prevent you from having a Social Lunar, though. I'll be doing my best to have more social combat in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:30:45-07:00","id":158067,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/Dragon%20Quest%203%20LP%20Update%205/ProfessorSalzbourg.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Because I have so many ideas, and because you all have next to no idea what's in the Spiral, I'll let you all field questions to Enien about the workings and happenings of the Spiral. Know, however, that her knowledge is not absolute, and she's largely not been in the West, where you are. <br /> <br /> Also, since you all haven't gotten Exp in, like, 2 months, I'll grant you all 10 exp, in addition to rewards for good role-playing and stunts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T11:34:31-07:00","id":158071,"title":"","content":"Professor Salzbourg:<br /> <br /> What types of Awesome Kung-Fu styles (aside from Titanic Hero style, of course) are practiced in the Spiral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T16:42:57-07:00","id":158405,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg1.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I assume you mean the regimented and codified styles of fighting, because otherwise, your question would get a ridiculous answer. As you say, there is Titanic Hero, and of course, Black Claw, the style I trained under Peerless Ocelot in. However, there are many, many more.<br /> <br /> To wit, there are as many martial arts in the Spiral as there are stars in the Sky-vault, if not more. I have heard of innumerable ones, but my personal favorites are as such:<br /> <br /> Impossible Black Quill Style: A Terrestrial style that revolves around manipulating your hair, especially into hardened dagger-style quills. Nasty stuff.<br /> <br /> Terrifying Hungry Wolf Style: A Celestial style formed by the many predatory Titans, it involves losing oneself to instinct and using your teeth and fingers to violent effect. I'm not a fan, but I've seen it used to great effect at the Battle of Loarn.<br /> <br /> Zeni-Jutsu: A martial art used by the Guild, which involves the weaponizing of the black nachre coins they're fond of, along with using paper scrip as a thrown weapon. It can also transform fallen foes into cash.<br /> <br /> Awe-Inspiring Shadowy Cavern Style: A Sidereal style that alloows you to summon objects from your mind, using Ignorance itself as a weapon Supposedly, Cytherea lent this Style to her Exalts, the Philosophers.<br /> <br /> And of course, Septimal Aesthete of Wonder style, a style I hope to initiate into one day, that manipulates the Limit of what is and what-is-not. It emulates the Principle of Oramus, my master, you see. I've seen it used drive men, gods and Daeva alike to ruin, or to save entire systems from total destruction. However, I'm not that far along into enlightenemnt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T17:50:49-07:00","id":158457,"title":"","content":"Sorry to distract from the awesomeness that is Professor Salzbourg, but I've been a bit lazy with keeping up with exp rewards since the game began. Saving myself a bit of screening through the thread (threads?), has anyone else been paying attention? If not, I'll happily take one for the team and do some accounting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-03T18:01:02-07:00","id":158464,"title":"","content":"I think where at 17 exp total now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T08:22:39-07:00","id":159075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jotun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=158457#post158457\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry to distract from the awesomeness that is Professor Salzbourg, but I've been a bit lazy with keeping up with exp rewards since the game began. Saving myself a bit of screening through the thread (threads?), has anyone else been paying attention? If not, I'll happily take one for the team and do some accounting.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're at 18 experience now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T11:56:35-07:00","id":159250,"title":"","content":"Professor!<br /> <br /> Where might Wren find leads on getting people somewhere they can stop running?<br /> <br /> Where might he run into temptation with this and trouble?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T14:34:21-07:00","id":159359,"title":"","content":"Are the Rusemin dead or alive ?<br /> <br /> Miss Enien are there planets that resists the primordial and their servants ? And what is the most advanced race in the spiral ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T18:09:07-07:00","id":159576,"title":"","content":"The Rusemin are alive, Magnusar.<br /> <br /> Also!<br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg2.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Places to gather information? Well, I assume you want population centers or trade transit hubs, then? Well, in the West, they have the center of the Guild, the Celestial Nexus of Luxury, where Ta'akozoka, the Many Tentacled One, is said to reside. There's also Mose Verten, a decommissioned battle-station far more spire-ward than we are. That's a hub of commercial traffic and is something of a tourist trap, especially for the Baffe Clan, a human-esque race. Finally, there's Ev Ilta's Paradise, a planet close to the Spire, a sort of amusement park planet made for Exalts and Peers. I went there once. I lost thirteen obols and resolved to never gamble while inebriated again.<br /> <br /> If we're talking more in the South, where I lived for most of my life, I'd say the Scarlet Gem of the Southern Seas, a trade planet that harvests the Fire-Spice that fuels Cecylene's war industries. There's also the Patient Lap of the Eternal Saint, a shrine-planet to the Mountain of Perfection. I like the latter. A cute little place, and they have the nicest bonsai gardens.<br /> <br /> As for temptation? Well, most of those places cater to the basest pursuits and hobbies you can imagine. It'd be hard to answer that, unless you get more specific. Also, I'd recommend not to get indebted to the Guild. They'll have their pound of flesh, sooner or later.<br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg3.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Of course there's resistance! The Incarnae left a bad precedent, and rebellions erupt every so often. The War of Loarn that I mentioned before was one such attempt. Most rebellions occur in the East, though. The Regional Shogun has been cracking down too hard, and she's probably going to be reprimanded soon for being overbearing.<br /> <br /> As for the most powerful species in the Spiral, that'd definitely be the Ba'alin, Theion's personal servant species. After getting so betrayed by the Dragon Kings, he resolved to learn from his mistake, and make them beholden to Him alone. They are, as a species, usually about 2.5 meters tall, and how to describe them? Well, they have human bodies, leonine faces, caprine horns, two sets of arms, and a tail. They also have patches of fur on their legs and back that make them look poofier than they are. Ba'alin are haughty, proud creatures, and they possess a labyrinthine sense of honor and indebtedness. I recommend being as honest and as forthright with one as you can, if you see them. Oh, and don't underestimate or insult them. They're hard as hell to kill, and their guns are nasty works of business.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1586,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","user":"Dietaku","date":". 06-05-2014, 12:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T18:57:03-07:00","id":159591,"title":"","content":"The Ba'alin sounds pretty nasty but I would like to meet one if only to test if they really hard to kill.<br /> <br /> It is good to know that we could meet allies against the primordials, speeking of primordial is there one residing in this arm of the spiral or do they all live in the same place ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T20:29:41-07:00","id":159685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnusar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=159591#post159591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">speeking of primordial is there one residing in this arm of the spiral<br /> <br /> or<br /> <br /> do they all live in the same place ?</div> </div> </div> </div>These statements are not mutually contradictory. Primordials have multiple Joten, or bodies that each entirely express them. So the Demon City and the Brass Dance are both Malfeas in his entirety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-04T22:05:55-07:00","id":159742,"title":"","content":"Dear Professor/Enien: what sort of criminal organizations exist generally throughout the Spiral? Nothing quasi-legal (ex this Guild) but along the lines of pirates, organized crime, mercenary companies, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2059-jotun","name":"Jotun","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T13:57:13-07:00","id":160228,"title":"","content":"Professor, to clarify:<br /> The way to a home without running Wren seeks-one way or another. What would be a potentially <i>bad</i> way to go about it? How may he be tempted in that endeavor to an 'easier' or more expedient answer to the problem of finding a home to truly rest in?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1148-palemask","name":"Palemask","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T15:18:51-07:00","id":160310,"title":"","content":"<img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg4.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Mr. X. Thalion is correct: several Titans have sections of their Soul Hierarchies, Joutens and the like, in several places at once. As for the ones in the West, last I checked, Ta'akozoka, the Many-Tentacles One is present in Her Capital in Nexus of Luxury. There's also Capura, the Goat at the Crossroads of Time, who lives in a promontory in the far West. Kimberry, the Sea that Marches against the Flame, makes Her capital in the Elemental Pole of Water, and, depending on how you draw the line at where the &quot;West&quot; ends, Maanus, the Alabaster Effigy of Glamor, lives to the far North of our current position on a planet devoted to Himself.<br /> <br /> The Pyre of all Knowledge used to live in the West, but she's had a project in the Center for about two centuries now, and no one's sure of what She's doing. <br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg5.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> There are as many criminals as there are laws of Cecylene, if not more! I'm not entirely familiar with the criminal syndicates of the West, because I haven't really lived there, and I doubt knowing about the Murderous Brotherhood of the All-Seeing Eye would help much, when they're not here.<br /> <br /> However, there IS a Pirate fleet I know of; a band of buccaneers who wave the flag of a red, winged cog. They call themselves the Pirates of the Star of Disaster, and make their fleets in the planet-sized husk of the dead god Najuu. According to what I know, an evil aura extends over Najuu, thanks to an ancient Exalt who did battle with the god, the Alchemical named Swift Proton Miria. She battled Najuu for a week during the campaign you all know of as the Great Retreat. However, the battle supposedly killed them both, and now Najuu's body is cursed with ill tidings, and these buccaneers are one such symptom, holding fast over their ideology, claiming that an &quot;Angel in Red&quot; came to them, commanding them to take up arms. Reports make the figure to look about like this, but I don't know if that's helpful at all or not.<br /> <img src=\"http://i880.photobucket.com/albums/ac10/Dietaku/ProfessorSalzbourg6.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> I dunno. I sense there's a loaded question in there. I suppose the worst way would be to get yourself killed, but that <i>would</i> prevent you from running, so that would technically fulfill your motivation. I suppose being stripped of all free will would be bad, too, which makes becoming an akuma of the Pyre a bad idea. However, to become an akuma, you'd have to have performed some huge service to the Titan in question, so, that would be difficult, given your current circumstances. However, you mention temptation. I'm not sure, if its just my experience or if this is true of all Titans, but most are not in the habit of making themselves seem weak to appeal to mortals, even Exalts. Not that they WON'T; Capura is enamored with love and its effect on people, but I don't know Capura personally. You'd have to ask Her yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T16:38:26-07:00","id":160361,"title":"","content":"Well Let's hope we don't come across any of them. Did I miss something, Exthalion finished is character ?! where is it ? o.O<br /> <br /> Also Dietaku where do you get the drawing of Enien do you make them yourself ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","user":"Magnusar","date":". 06-05-2014, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T16:49:53-07:00","id":160370,"title":"","content":"Exthalion's character has been finished for a few days. He just hasn't posted it yet, probably because I had yet to introduce him.<br /> <br /> I get the Enien drawings from <a href=\"http://pochi.lix.jp/k_kisekae2.html\" target=\"_blank\">here (Warning: NSFW)</a> which is a pretty neat dress-up game.<br /> <br /> I WOULD draw Enien myself, but I lack a tablet, so there's that. Which is also why I haven't done an Exalted comic series yet :|.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T17:17:42-07:00","id":160395,"title":"","content":"Pretty neat game not my thing but neat and useful. Well at least you can draw and since we saw Enien, Zephyr and Radical Mendicat Zekka I thought I would put the image I used to make Amelia, I find that visual references help to created the character so here it is <a href=\"http://peterprime.deviantart.com/art/OC-Battle-Beatrix-143031116\" target=\"_blank\">http://peterprime.deviantart.com/art...trix-143031116</a> I think it looks pretty badass<br /> <br /> Miss Enien are there solars in the spiral that are not under the control of the Titans ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2087-magnusar","name":"Magnusar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"458"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T18:35:08-07:00","id":160440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/56130-ooc-exalted-2-5-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=160370#post160370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exthalion's character has been finished for a few days. He just hasn't posted it yet, probably because I had yet to introduce him.<br /> <br /> I get the Enien drawings from <a href=\"http://pochi.lix.jp/k_kisekae2.html\" target=\"_blank\">here (Warning: NSFW)</a> which is a pretty neat dress-up game.<br /> <br /> I WOULD draw Enien myself, but I lack a tablet, so there's that. Which is also why I haven't done an Exalted comic series yet :|.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is might just be me, but that looks a remarkably like K-on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-05T21:27:20-07:00","id":160560,"title":"","content":"That is indeed K-ON! I think the series is alright by itself, but the game has astounding variation in faces and hairstyles, so I find it useful for modeling female characters. or if I'm bored and seeing what I can make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-06T19:33:37-07:00","id":161345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kelsyk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/60177-ic-exalted-gunstar-to-boldly-go?p=160936#post160936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OOC:<br /> My RPG background is mostly Living Forgotten Realms with GMs who are actually aiming for TPK so a GM's attitude of &quot;GM versus Player&quot; is fairly routine for me, at least in terms of combat</div> </div> </div> </div>I assure you, as a fellow PC who has played under Dietaku innumerable times, that he has never tried to actively TPK anyone. Doesn't mean that we won't get TPK'd, but if it does, it's because of a gross miscalculation on our parts, a gross miscalculation on his part, or because the Loom of Fate decided to screw us over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/155-noodle","name":"Noodle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar155_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1415"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T10:09:19-07:00","id":162489,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Okay, here is my sheet. If anyone has any advice I would greatly appreciate it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Name:</b> Ieremiel of the Gate</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Caste:</b> Pyrian Sovereign</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Motivation:</b><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Reform the Perfected </span></span>Hierarchy<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> to elevate Humanity and its Exalted.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Appearance:</b> Pale, lean, and hairless with watery blue eyes and skin so thin it is almost see through. At least, that is how his corpses have always looked. No one has ever seen him alive outside his faceless armor.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Personality:</b> Quiet, slow to consider the opinions of others, more benevolent then he will admit, quick to take offense but slow to show it</span></span></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backstory</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> He of the shining wings, he of the turning wheel, he who was of old; he, O people, is Ieremiel.<br /> The Pyre drew him forth from the fundament, clean of Mankind's Disobedience, and the Holy one most highly exalted him to sovereign purpose.<br /> Warden of the Threshold, architect of ineffable design, who holds the sword and the compass; he, ye multitude, is Ieremiel.<br /> When he flies by the swift road, Kai, who stands before the Cave of Yesterdays, commands him halt and return, for his his task is yet undone.<br /> Last of the first men and first of the new, who takes birth with open eyes, in whom the Titans are well pleased; he, ye slaves, is Ieremiel.<br /> <br /> Much he did in repentance of war. Towers he raised and Isidorus toppled them. Gardens he planted and the Pyre razed them. Temple he hallowed and the Chaos smote them.<br /> Secret author of new Disobedience, weary of labor to another's design, who nurtures rebellion in his heart; he, o traitors, is Ieremiel.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">In the wake of the Great Revolt, Theion began to call for the destruction of all mankind as punishment for daring to rise up against the Primordials and obliteration of their souls for the crime of wounding them. Believing her king was about to commit a grave error, the Principle of Hierarchy exerted her magic against the world and drew forth seven mortals, body and soul, clean of even the suspicion of rebellion. She held them up to the Universe Emperor as the first humans to be unmade. Entranced by the promise of this new race of men the Empyreal Chaos left his command unfinished, willing to wait and see what came. The surrender of the Sun and the rise of the Titanic Exalt seem to have borne out the wisdom of the Pyrian Flame. As for her seven mortals, they became among the first of the Sovereigns.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">So great was their service to the Spiral that it was commanded that they should never have respite. Their souls were marked with sorcerous brands that forced them to turn back from Lethe into waiting bodies. Each has built a mighty legend in their lifetimes of labor for the Titans and against their enemies. Among them was Ieremiel, and the love the humans of the spiral feel for him is equaled only by the hate of the Autochthonian Realm for so great a traitor to his race.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Yet, Ieremiel has grown tired of lifetimes without respite, the eternal withering and flowering of enlightenment and power, and the suffering of endless war. His recent incarnations have focused on more peaceful tasks, such as creating the post-human deva species known as the Atmanatta and promoting harmony between humanity and the other servant races. For ages he forced himself to be blind to race, yet the continued </span></span>penance<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> of mankind has begun to anger him. Though he long ago ceased to consider himself human, they remain without patronage or intercession.</span></span></span></span><br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stats</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><u>Attributes</u></b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Strength \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dexterity \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stamina \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Charisma \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Manipulation \u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Appearance \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Perception \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Intelligence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wits \u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b><u>Abilities</u></b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Archery</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Martial Arts</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Melee </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thrown</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(c)War</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(c)Integrity \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(c)Performance</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(f)Presence \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Resistance</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Survival</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(f)Craft \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Investigation</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(f)Lore \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf (Gunstar +1)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Medicine</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(f)Occult \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf (Telepresence +3)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(c)Awareness \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Athletics</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dodge</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Larceny</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stealth </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(c)Bureaucracy</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Linguistics (+Old Realm)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ride </span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sail</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">(f)Socialize \u25cf</span></span></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Charms</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Theion</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">First Theion Excellency x5</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sorcerous Enlightenment of Theion</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Ultimate Sovereign Fundament</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">King of All Kings Numen</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Imperishable Majesty Stance</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Empyrean Mandate Tongue</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cosmic Tyrant Degree</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Cecelyne</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Transcendent Desert Creature</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>She Who Lives in Her Name</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Factual Determination Analysis</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Essence-Dissecting Stare</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mind-Hand Manipulation</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Tool-Transcending Construct</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><i>Terrestrial Circle Spells</i></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Slave Spawn Summoning</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Virtuous Guardian of Flame</span></span></span></span> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backgrounds/Panoply</span></span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Backgrounds:</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Wealth \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cult \u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Backing \u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Influence \u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Artifact \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Sorcery \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Manse \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Panoply Description:</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Armor of Iremiel (Sanctified Jade Superheavy Plate)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">For almost everyone how knows of him, and for the Sovereign himself, this armor is the face of Iremiel. Its white jade plates flash like mother of pearl in the light, its orichalcum ornamentation is pale as electrum and bright as a mirror, and the closed face of its crown-like helm obscures the face behind from even the closest inspection. Many suits like it are hung in the treasure vaults of the Gunstar and every one had to be cut away from the corpses within for this armor is not meant to be removed. In womb-sarcophagi deep in the spiral, soulless effigies are fitted with the the raw plates and baptized in Theion-To to bring both artifacts to completion. So it is that the Titanic Exalted who wears it has never seen what lies within.</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stone of the Sannyasa (As Stone of the Malfean Elemental, aligned to the post-human deva species known as the Atmanatta)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The most visible sign of Iremiel's work is the Atmanatta. Though each was born as a human, they have left that state behind to become some of the most highly favored deva races. They seek out the greatest of mortals, the sort who might have been Exalted in other circumstances, and refine them in the crucible of wisdom and </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">enlightenment</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. The many paths of transcendence have led to many varieties of Atmanatta, distinct only in </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">appearance</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> and philosophy. The most common appear as they did as mortals save with bones of pale crystal, muscle and veins spun from lightning, skin of cold blue fire, and wings like plasma arcs. Some have bodies of rippling mercury, others are </span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">silhouettes</span></span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> shaped from clouds of dust and full of stars, and still others are shimmering ripples of solidified sound over skeletons of hardened light. (Use the statistics of the T</span></span></span></span>eodojzia for convenience<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">)</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Intimacies:</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Atmanatta (Proud Affection)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Titans (Exasperated Loyalty)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Gunstar (Wary Interest)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">His Own Cycle of Reincarnation (Fearful Weariness)</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Virtues:</b></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Valor \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Conviction \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Compassion \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Temperance \u25cf\u25cf</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Virtue Flaw/Curse:</b> Conviction</span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><b>Urge:</b> Build a human empire more glorious than the Traitor Realm to prove 